{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bro2ahmy0","tool_use_id":"toolu_018tf9itjN6rrsMLPY6vNCWw","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/3e4952aa-339a-41f3-bd4e-e95b2fa473d3/tasks/bro2ahmy0.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_1\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nPeople judge randomness by running a gambler's-fallacy predictor through the sequence: before each flip they expect the coin to \"correct\" the heads/tails imbalance seen so far, with recent flips weighing more than older ones in that leaky running tally, and a sequence looks random to the extent its flips match those corrective expectations (high average predictive probability). Unlike the incumbent's position-blind balance and alternation summaries, this makes the *order* of flips matter — a terminal repeat or a late streak (which violates a strong, just-built expectation of reversal) is penalised far more than the same repeat early on — so the two models disagree most on equal-composition pairs that differ only in where a repeat or run sits, especially at the end; people also differ in how sharply they apply this judgment.\nEOF\necho gamblers_fallacy_leaky_predictor > $D/model_name.txt\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/candidate.py\n\"\"\"Gambler's-fallacy leaky predictor.\n\nPeople judge randomness by running a gambler's-fallacy predictor through the\nsequence: before each flip they expect the coin to correct the heads/tails\nimbalance seen so far, with recent flips weighing more than older ones in a\nleaky running tally. A sequence looks random to the extent its flips match\nthose corrective expectations (high average log predictive probability), so\nthe order of flips matters: a late repeat or streak, violating a just-built\nexpectation of reversal, is penalised more than the same pattern early on.\nPeople differ in how sharply they apply the judgment (person-level\nsensitivity).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pymc as pm\nimport pytensor.tensor as pt\n\nMAX_LEN = 8\nN_SLOTS = 400\n\n\ndef _encode(seq):\n    s = seq.strip().upper()\n    x = np.zeros(MAX_LEN)\n    for i, c in enumerate(s):\n        x[i] = 1.0 if c == \"H\" else -1.0\n    return x, len(s)\n\n\ndef compute_features(sequence_a, sequence_b):\n    xa, na = _encode(sequence_a)\n    xb, nb = _encode(sequence_b)\n    feats = {}\n    for i in range(MAX_LEN):\n        feats[f\"xa_{i}\"] = float(xa[i])\n        feats[f\"xb_{i}\"] = float(xb[i])\n    feats[\"len_a\"] = float(na)\n    feats[\"len_b\"] = float(nb)\n    return feats\n\n\n# Lag-exponent matrix: tally before flip t uses flips j < t weighted lambda^(t-1-j).\n_E = np.zeros((MAX_LEN, MAX_LEN))\n_M = np.zeros((MAX_LEN, MAX_LEN))\nfor _t in range(MAX_LEN):\n    for _j in range(_t):\n        _E[_t, _j] = _t - 1 - _j\n        _M[_t, _j] = 1.0\n\n\ndef _score(X, length, lam, g):\n    # X: (trials, MAX_LEN) of +-1 (0 padding); flips t >= 1 and t < length count.\n    L = pt.as_tensor_variable(_M) * lam ** pt.as_tensor_variable(_E)\n    tally = pt.dot(X, L.T)  # leaky H-minus-T tally before each flip\n    # Predicted P(actual flip) = sigmoid(-g * tally * x_t): expectation of reversal.\n    logp = pt.log(pm.math.sigmoid(-g * tally * X))\n    pos = pt.arange(MAX_LEN)[None, :]\n    valid = pt.and_(pt.ge(pos, 1), pt.lt(pos, length[:, None]))\n    valid = pt.cast(valid, \"float64\")\n    return pt.sum(logp * valid, axis=1) / pt.maximum(pt.sum(valid, axis=1), 1.0)\n\n\nwith pm.Model() as model:\n    xa = pt.stack(\n        [pm.Data(f\"xa_{i}\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\")) for i in range(MAX_LEN)],\n        axis=1,\n    )\n    xb = pt.stack(\n        [pm.Data(f\"xb_{i}\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\")) for i in range(MAX_LEN)],\n        axis=1,\n    )\n    len_a = pm.Data(\"len_a\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    len_b = pm.Data(\"len_b\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n\n    # Strength of the expected correction per unit of tally.\n    g = pm.LogNormal(\"g\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.75)\n    # Memory leak: 0 = only the last flip matters, 1 = full running balance.\n    lam = pm.Beta(\"lam\", alpha=2.0, beta=2.0)\n\n    # Person-level sensitivity (non-centred, log scale).\n    mu_log_beta = pm.Normal(\"mu_log_beta\", mu=1.5, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_log_beta = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_log_beta\", sigma=0.75)\n    z = pm.Normal(\"z\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=N_SLOTS)\n    beta_p = pt.exp(mu_log_beta + sigma_log_beta * z)\n\n    side_bias = pm.Normal(\"side_bias\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.5)\n\n    score_a = _score(xa, len_a, lam, g)\n    score_b = _score(xb, len_b, lam, g)\n\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\",\n        pm.math.sigmoid(beta_p[participant_id] * (score_a - score_b) + side_bias),\n    )\n    chose_left = pm.Data(\"chose_left\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n    pm.Bernoulli(\"response\", p=p_left, observed=chose_left)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses $D/../../responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -15\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"ea2a0523-fdb8-43fc-9fa6-368e32e87664","session_id":"3e4952aa-339a-41f3-bd4e-e95b2fa473d3"}
